  "output": "Based on the code shown (and consistent with prior audits of this repo), here are concrete, actionable findings:\n\n## 1. Caching opportunities\n\n**`src/utils/cache.ts`** already has a localStorage cache layer, but it's under-used. Two gaps:\n\n- `cacheGet`/`cacheSet` do a full `JSON.parse`/`JSON.stringify` on every call with no in-memory tier — for frequently-read keys (e.g. platform settings, phrase categories) this reparses on every access.\n- `pruneOldCache()` runs unconditionally on module load (`src/utils/cache.ts:29`), iterating **all** of `localStorage` synchronously at import time — on every page load, not just once. This is wasted work if there's nothing to prune. Cheap fix: gate it behind a one-time flag:\n\n```ts\nconst PRUNE_FLAG = 'jd-vb:pruned';\nif (!window.sessionStorage.getItem(PRUNE_FLAG)) {\n  pruneOldCache();\n  window.sessionStorage.setItem(PRUNE_FLAG, '1');\n}\n```\n\n- `src/api.ts`'s `request()` has no caching at all — every call to `bots()`, `campaigns()`, `phrases()`, etc. hits the network. Reference data (phrase categories, outcome rules, language settings) rarely changes within a session and could use a simple TTL cache wrapping `request`.\n\n## 2. Redundant computations\n\n- `src/utils/transcript.ts:buildConversationItems` filters `events` and rebuilds/sorts arrays from scratch every call. If this is called on every render of a transcript-detail view (each keystroke/poll), wrap the call site in `useMemo` keyed on `[transcript, events]`.\n- `src/utils/formatting.ts:parseApiDate` runs a regex test (`hasTimezone`) on every call to `formatDate`/`formatTime`/`timeAgo` — for tables rendering hundreds of rows (transcripts, audit log), this regex + `new Date()` + `toLocaleString` with `Intl` options runs per-cell per-render. `toLocaleString` with options objects is comparatively expensive; consider hoisting a single `Intl.DateTimeFormat` instance:\n\n```ts\nconst DATE_FMT = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-IN', { dateStyle: 'medium', timeStyle: 'short', timeZone: 'Asia/Kolkata' });\nexport function formatDate(value?: string) {\n  if (!value) return '-';\n  const date = parseApiDate(value);\n  if (Number.isNaN(date.getTime())) return value;\n  return `${DATE_FMT.format(date)} IST`;\n}\n```\nThis avoids re-parsing the formatter options on every call — meaningful in list views with many rows.\n\n## 3. Unnecessary React re-renders\n\n- `src/hooks/useToasts.ts` — fine as-is (properly memoized with `useCallback`).\n- `src/hooks/useKeyboardShortcuts.ts` already uses the refs pattern correctly to avoid re-registering listeners — good example, no issue.\n- Known issue from prior audits (memory obs #1389/#1612): **`TranscriptsView`** re-renders its full list on every parent state change because filtered/derived arrays aren't memoized, and **`App.tsx`** (1173 lines) has multiple `useEffect`s that fire sequentially causing cascading re-renders on auth. Since `App.tsx` wasn't in the excerpt given here, I'd need to open it directly to give line-specific fixes — flag if you want me to pull it via the graph tool (`get_review_context`) rather than reading the whole file.\n\n## 4. Memory leaks\n\n- `src/hooks/useCountUp.ts` — the `requestAnimationFrame` loop is not cancelled on unmount; only `duration`/`target` changes cancel implicitly by starting over via `useEffect` cleanup being absent. Fix:\n\n```ts\nuseEffect(() => {\n  if (target === 0) { setValue(0); return; }\n  let rafId: number;\n  const start = performance.now();\n  ref.current?.classList.add('counting');\n  const tick = (now: number) => {\n    const progress = Math.min((now - start) / duration, 1);\n    const eased = 1 - Math.pow(1 - progress, 3);\n    setValue(Math.round(target * eased));\n    if (progress < 1) rafId = requestAnimationFrame(tick);\n    else ref.current?.classList.remove('counting');\n  };\n  rafId = requestAnimationFrame(tick);\n  return () => cancelAnimationFrame(rafId);\n}, [target, duration]);\n```\nWithout this, unmounting a component mid-animation (e.g. navigating away from a dashboard stat tile) leaks a dangling RAF callback that calls `setState` on an unmounted component.\n\n- `src/hooks/useToasts.ts` uses `setTimeout(() => dismissToast(id), durationMs)` with no stored timeout id / cleanup — if the component unmounts before the timer fires, `dismissToast` still runs (harmless here since it's a functional setState, but the timer itself isn't cleared, so it fires late and wastes a tick). Low severity but trivial to fix by tracking timeout IDs in a ref and clearing them in a `useEffect` cleanup if `useToasts` is ever used with a short-lived component tree.\n\n## 5. N+1 query patterns\n\nNone in the frontend snippets shown here — `src/api.ts`'s `request<T>` is a single fetch per call, and the types (`Transcript`, `CallEvent`, `AuditLogEntry`) suggest list+detail fetches are already batched server-side. The N+1-shaped issues in this codebase are backend (`callback_worker`, analytics aggregation in Python) — already logged in earlier audits (obs #1392, #1609: analytics endpoints do in-memory aggregation instead of Mongo pipelines). That's out of scope for `frontend/` alone.\n\n---\n**Priority order:** RAF leak in `useCountUp` (real leak) → gate `pruneOldCache()` to run once (waste on every load) → memoize `buildConversationItems` call sites → hoist `Intl.DateTimeFormat` instances in `formatting.ts`.\n\nWant me to open `App.tsx` and `TranscriptsView` directly to give line-specific memoization fixes for the re-render issues, since those weren't in the provided excerpt?\n",
